{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s fund-distribution setting.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u1.497"},{"reason":"Describes added features; does not make every added feature a gift.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u2.512"},{"reason":"Describes standing-instruction services, not an additional gift-control condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u3.792"},{"reason":"Marketing background; public or aggressive marketing is not required by the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u4.1115"},{"reason":"Guaranteed-returns heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u5.1267"},{"reason":"Identifies a separate statutory control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u6.1287"},{"reason":"Explains fund returns and distributor top-ups; relevant to classification but not a categorical gift definition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"reason":"Potential structured-product classification is separate from gift classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u8.1651"},{"reason":"Separate offence, authorisation and exemption provisions; their exceptions do not attach to the gift control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u9.1940"},{"reason":"Disclosure and misleading-impression concerns remain separate controls.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u10.2239"},{"reason":"Identifies paragraph 3.11 as the selected control’s source.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u11.2603"},{"reason":"Gift scrutiny remains relevant without structured-product status; classification is conditional.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"reason":"Operative gift control, discount exception, promotion connection and product-type examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"reason":"Connects separate section 103 and paragraph 3.11 restrictions without categorically banning all incentives.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"},{"reason":"Separate dealing-frequency heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u15.4022"},{"reason":"Observed redemption restrictions concern a separate control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u16.4063"},{"reason":"Fairness and redemption duties are outside the selected gift control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u17.4359"},{"reason":"Administrative procedures and best-endeavours dealing requirements do not qualify the gift prohibition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u18.4879"},{"reason":"Separate marketing heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u19.5230"},{"reason":"Misleading-advertisement and paragraph 2.3 requirements remain independently relevant.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u20.5257"},{"reason":"Advertising-guideline dependency belongs to a separate advertising control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u21.5903"},{"reason":"Risk and deposit-comparison restrictions are separate advertising controls.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u22.6374"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible future action supply no selected-control effective date or additional exception.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u23.7007"},{"reason":"Institutional signature.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u24.7186"},{"reason":"Institutional signature.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u25.7275"},{"reason":"Institutional signature.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u26.7393"},{"reason":"Footnote supports the separate offering-document disclosure requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u27.7511"},{"reason":"Identifies the Code’s full title, including licensed and registered persons.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u28.7987"},{"reason":"Identifies relevant FAQ question and issue date; the answer itself is absent and cannot resolve the connection threshold.","status":"UNCERTAIN","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u29.8110"},{"reason":"Supplementary advertising guidance is referenced but not supplied; it concerns the separate advertising control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u30.8235"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"Evaluate an individual benefit offer by an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds to a client. The opening reference to licensed corporations’ observed practices does not itself exclude registered distributors. Paragraph 10 uses broader investment-product language; application beyond the circular’s fund setting remains unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u28.7987"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Gift is not exhaustively defined. Guaranteed returns and other incentives may qualify, rather than automatically qualifying. Product types expressly include funds grouped by type or fund house. Neither the precise linkage threshold nor the treatment of rebates and mixed benefits is supplied.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fees-or-charges discount parenthesis qualifies gifts and carries through the later reference to such gifts. It does not excuse separate non-discount gifts. Section 103 authorisation and exemptions attach to that separate statutory control, not paragraph 3.11.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u14.3675"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected control states should not offer and calls itself a requirement. Proposed Boolean results flag conduct contrary to that control; they do not classify it as the separate statutory offence. Actual receipt, investment, or demonstrated distraction is not stated as necessary. May be considered leaves gift classification open.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"No effective date, expiry or transition rule for the selected control is supplied. 2010-09-30 is the cited FAQ’s issue date, not an established commencement date. The control concerns the offer in its promotional setting.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u23.7007","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The paragraph 3.11 quotation and the referenced FAQ support the selected control, but the full Code and FAQ answer are absent. Structured-product status is not a prerequisite for gift scrutiny. Other disclosure, redemption and advertising duties remain independent of the selected result.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u11.2603","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u14.3675","db43e253bea18.u17.4359","db43e253bea18.u20.5257","db43e253bea18.u21.5903","db43e253bea18.u27.7511","db43e253bea18.u28.7987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110","db43e253bea18.u30.8235"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the cited FAQ treat product-type linkage as sufficient by itself, or require a separate finding that the offer promotes that product type?","What distinguishes a fees-or-charges discount from a cash rebate, distributor-funded top-up or mixed promotional package?","What actor and product coverage does the full paragraph 3.11 establish beyond this circular’s SFC-authorised-fund setting?","Which version and effective period of paragraph 3.11 and the cited FAQ govern the assessed offer?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The assessment unit is one benefit offered to one client; separate benefits in a package require separate assessment.","Both alternatives use the circular’s defined distributor population as a common bounded scope.","A product-type linkage is substantive; its existence requires assessment of the offer’s terms and presentation.","The discount exception continues to apply to gifts mentioned in the final sentence.","Unknown classification or connection facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"}],"distinction":"Product-type linkage is sufficient to bring an otherwise qualifying gift offer within the control, even without a separately established promotional finding. This gives operative force to the final sentence’s if/then formulation. The strongest uncertainty is what linkage must comprise; the missing FAQ may make promotional connection intrinsic to that concept.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, within the circular’s distributor definition.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u28.7987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The actor offers the assessed benefit to a client; acceptance or payment is not required.","name":"offers_benefit_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a gift for paragraph 3.11, considering that returns and incentives may, but need not, qualify.","name":"is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception; this does not classify separate benefits in the same package.","name":"is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to the client, assessed separately from mere product-type linkage.","name":"has_promotional_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The manner of offering the assessed benefit links it to a particular investment-product type, including certain fund types or funds offered by particular fund houses.","name":"has_product_type_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and is_gift (not is_fee_or_charge_discount) (or has_promotional_connection has_product_type_link))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor offers_benefit_to_client)"},"local_id":"reading_link_sufficient","questions":["Can a benefit be linked to a product type without being offered in promoting that type, and does the FAQ address that case?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] For the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control, within the stated actor-and-offer scope, true means the assessed benefit is a gift, is not a fees-or-charges discount, and either has the specified promotional connection or is offered in a manner linking it to a particular investment-product type. Actual investor distraction need not be proved. This is a proposed reading of the selected control only.","subject":"Paragraph-10 gift control: product-type linkage as a sufficient connection"},{"assumptions":["The assessment unit is one benefit offered to one client; separate benefits in a package require separate assessment.","Both alternatives use the circular’s defined distributor population as a common bounded scope.","The final sentence illustrates the first sentence’s promotion requirement and retains that requirement.","The discount exception continues to apply to gifts mentioned in the final sentence.","Unknown classification or connection facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"The purpose of the requirement is to avoid the use of gifts to distract investors from the features and risks of a particular product.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u29.8110"}],"distinction":"A promotional connection remains necessary in every case; product-type linkage supports that finding but is not an independent trigger. If linkage is established and promotion is affirmatively absent, this alternative does not flag the offer while the first does. This reading is less secure against the final sentence’s express if/then wording; the referenced but absent FAQ is the strongest unresolved dependency.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, within the circular’s distributor definition.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u28.7987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The actor offers the assessed benefit to a client; acceptance or payment is not required.","name":"offers_benefit_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a gift for paragraph 3.11, considering that returns and incentives may, but need not, qualify.","name":"is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception; this does not classify separate benefits in the same package.","name":"is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to the client, assessed separately from mere product-type linkage.","name":"has_promotional_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The manner of offering the assessed benefit links it to a particular investment-product type, including certain fund types or funds offered by particular fund houses.","name":"has_product_type_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and is_gift (not is_fee_or_charge_discount) has_promotional_connection)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor offers_benefit_to_client)"},"local_id":"reading_promotion_required","questions":["Does the phrase this requirement carry the first sentence’s promotion condition into every linked-gift case, or does the final sentence establish linkage as sufficient?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] For the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control, within the stated actor-and-offer scope, true means the assessed benefit is a gift, is not a fees-or-charges discount, and is offered in promoting a specific investment product or particular product type. Linkage to a fund type or fund house informs the promotion assessment but does not replace it. Actual investor distraction need not be proved. This is a proposed reading of the selected control only.","subject":"Paragraph-10 gift control: promotional connection retained as a necessary condition"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s fund-distribution context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u1.497"},{"reason":"Observed additional features and restrictions; does not itself define gifts.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u2.512"},{"reason":"Standing-instruction services provide context for separate marketing requirements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u3.792"},{"reason":"Public marketing observations do not expressly limit the selected client-facing gift control to public campaigns.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u4.1115"},{"reason":"Guaranteed-returns heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u5.1267"},{"reason":"Identifies the separate statutory advertising provision.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u6.1287"},{"reason":"Describes fund returns and distributor top-ups; relevant to classifying an incentive but not a complete gift definition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u7.1360"},{"reason":"Conditional structured-product classification belongs to a separate control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u8.1651"},{"reason":"Separate public-invitation offence with authorisation and exemption qualifications; these are not gift-control exceptions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u9.1940"},{"reason":"Offering-document disclosures and misleading-impression concerns are separate from the selected gift control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u10.2239"},{"reason":"Identifies paragraph 3.11 as the selected control’s underlying reference.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u11.2603"},{"reason":"Gift assessment remains relevant even when an arrangement is not a structured product; classification is conditional.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"reason":"Primary selected rule, discount exception, promotional connection and product-type examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"reason":"Preserves the separate section 103 and paragraph 3.11 routes; does not prohibit every additional return unconditionally.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"},{"reason":"Heading for separate redemption controls.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u15.4022"},{"reason":"Observed lock-ups and reduced dealing frequency are outside the selected control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u16.4063"},{"reason":"Separate fairness and redemption duties are not formalized here.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u17.4359"},{"reason":"Administrative procedures and best-endeavours language concern dealing frequency, not an exception to the gift control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u18.4879"},{"reason":"Heading for separate marketing controls.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u19.5230"},{"reason":"Separate misleading-advertisement control and paragraph 2.3 dependency.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u20.5257"},{"reason":"Separate advertising-guideline dependency for service-return presentations.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u21.5903"},{"reason":"Separate restrictions on misleading return claims and deposit comparisons.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u22.6374"},{"reason":"Monitoring and possible regulatory action do not supply a commencement date or an additional gift exception.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u23.7007"},{"reason":"Departmental attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u24.7186"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u25.7275"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u26.7393"},{"reason":"Footnote 1 supports offering-document disclosures, a separate requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u27.7511"},{"reason":"Footnote 2 identifies the Code, including licensed and registered persons; full applicability provisions are absent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u28.7987"},{"reason":"Footnote 3 identifies the relevant FAQ and its issue date; its full answer and subsequent status are not supplied.","status":"UNCERTAIN","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u29.8110"},{"reason":"Footnote 4 identifies evolving advertising guidance, not a supplied modification of the gift control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u30.8235"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The proposed control concerns a distributor’s offer to a client connected with promoting a specific product or product type. This proposal stays within the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund context. Neither online distribution nor a public campaign is an express prerequisite. The quoted Code language refers more broadly to investment products, but its full actor and product applicability is not supplied.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u28.7987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Distributors are intermediaries distributing the funds. Gifts are not exhaustively defined. Guaranteed returns and other incentives may qualify, rather than qualifying automatically. Product types expressly include certain fund types and funds from certain fund houses. The boundary between a fee discount and a separate cash incentive remains unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-or-charge discount parenthesis attaches to gifts. It supplies no general exemption from advertising, redemption or statutory requirements. Section 103 authorisation and exemptions attach to the separate statutory invitation control.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u14.3675"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected rule says distributors 'should not' offer gifts and describes linked gifts as bound by the requirement. The proposed Boolean flags conduct falling within that stated prohibition; it does not label it a section 103 offence. 'May be considered a gift' preserves judgment about classification. Actual investor distraction is expressed as a rationale, not a separate factual prerequisite.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"No commencement, expiry or transition rule for the selected control is supplied. The FAQ issue date, 2010-09-30, is reference metadata and cannot be used as the control’s effective date. Temporal applicability must therefore be established separately.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u23.7007","db43e253bea18.u29.8110","db43e253bea18.u30.8235"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The selected control depends on paragraph 3.11 and the cited FAQ answer. Their complete text and applicable versions are absent. Structured-product classification and section 103 operate separately: a negative structured-product conclusion does not dispose of the gift question. Other Code, handbook and advertising references concern additional controls.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u8.1651","db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u11.2603","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u14.3675","db43e253bea18.u20.5257","db43e253bea18.u21.5903","db43e253bea18.u27.7511","db43e253bea18.u28.7987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110","db43e253bea18.u30.8235"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the applicable paragraph 3.11 or cited FAQ distinguish direct fee reductions, fee reimbursements and cash rebates, and whose fees or charges qualify?","What establishes the necessary promotional connection for a platform-wide or mixed-product campaign, including a campaign limited to one fund house?","Which version and effective period of paragraph 3.11 and FAQ answer 1 govern the assessed offer, and have later materials changed their application?","What additional applicability provisions determine the control’s reach beyond the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund distributors?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["Assess one identified benefit offered in one identified promotion; a mixed package requires separate classification of its components.","The proposal is limited to SFC-authorised-fund distribution and assumes temporal applicability has been established separately.","Gift status, discount status and promotional linkage remain supplied judgments; no unknown fact is assigned a truth value.","The packet supports one definite core reading. The treatment of rebates and indirect promotional links remains unresolved rather than being converted into unsupported competing rules."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u0.2"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u12.2646"},{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u13.2987"},{"quote":"in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u14.3675"},{"quote":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"db43e253bea18.u29.8110"}],"distinction":"The selected control turns on a non-exempt gift offered in a product-linked promotion. It is not an unconditional ban on every additional return, and it does not require either structured-product status or proof of actual distraction. Its strongest unresolved boundary is whether a particular monetary benefit genuinely constitutes a fee or charge discount; the supplied text does not settle rebate mechanics.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds in the activity under assessment.","name":"is_fund_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed actor offers the identified benefit to a client; acceptance or payment is not required for this fact.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered in promoting a specific fund or particular fund type, including a sufficient link to certain fund types or funds offered by certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift for the selected paragraph 3.11 control, before applying its fee-or-charge discount exception; guaranteed returns or incentives are not automatically classified as gifts.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the express exception; a cash-benefit label alone does not resolve this classification.","name":"benefit_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_or_charge_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_fund_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection)"},"local_id":"gift_control_1","questions":["Does a payment calculated by reference to fees qualify as a discount when it is paid separately or can exceed the fees?","What facts distinguish a general service promotion from a promotion linked to a particular investment product type?","Does the absent FAQ supply further gift classifications or qualifications?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] For the selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control, within the stated scope, true means the offered benefit is a gift falling outside the fee-or-charge discount exception and thus falls within the stated 'should not offer' requirement. False means only that this selected gift condition is not met; an out-of-scope offer is not assessed. Neither outcome establishes overall compliance or resolves section 103.","subject":"One distributor’s identified benefit offered to a client in a promotion connected with a specific SFC-authorised fund or fund type"}]}},"java_checks":[],"live_provider":true,"model_calls":2,"no_progress":0,"nodes":[],"pending":null,"provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1","retrievals":[],"rounds":0,"roundtrips":[],"run_id":"run.781bea33f5f74a90b622fee91a0d5e9e","stop":null}